# Everything here runs in Linux containers: LF on every platform, whatever
# core.autocrlf says (a Windows clone otherwise breaks every shebang).
* text=auto eol=lf

# Stacked pull requests each add lines at the same spot of the backlog and the
# ledger; the union driver keeps both sides' added lines in a local merge or
# rebase instead of stopping on a conflict (GitHub's own merge ignores it).
# A line both sides changed (a tick) survives twice: devhost-verify refuses a
# repeated backlog id, and the ledger append-only guard still reads the diff.
TODO.md merge=union
docs/ledger/*.md merge=union
